//!
//! The expected texts come from `tools/state_reference.py`, which builds the pedigree from
//! the model of `tools/world_reference.py`, written from the design note and not from this
//! code. Each case loads a save the reference pins (the scenarios of their own tests:
//! "step", "kin" and "neither" of `orphan_rule.rs`, "afflicted" of `afflictions.rs`,
//! "market" of `market.rs`) and compares the pedigree as `pedigree.json` holds it.
//! "loci" is a scenario of its own: seed 0xff, tag `test:loci2`, the repository's data, the
//! switch on, a woman with alleles at five disease loci and a man with three, both born
//! 30 years before the start, right after `Start`: the order of the loci and the diseases,
//! and a visible disease (`core:disease_mt`) affected at 30 with its onset at 27.3.

